Rationale: programs loaded into the Linux kernel via eBPF LSM hooks must be
GPL-compatible to use GPL-only helpers such as bpf_d_path. Declaring
GPL-2.0-only keeps us compatible with the kernel licensing requirements
regardless of the license used by the rest of the AgentGuard codebase.
